License: public domain, alternatively MIT (see upstream LICENSE.txt)

The upstream implementation is an optional runtime topology backend and a
conformance/performance reference. Its internal heap representation is not a
public Project Thessa contract; callers use the safe wrapper API.

Vendored for the optional FFI backend and conformance tooling (no upstream
implementation code copied into the project):
- third_party/libcbt/cbt.h (upstream, unmodified)
- third_party/libcbt/cbt_shim.c (project-owned plain-integer ABI shim)
- crates/rcbt-ffi (safe wrapper; serial and optional OpenMP entry points)
